  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930907",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-30873",
      "knowledge_point_id": "40eeb5a8-3ffe-54d2-b263-f2b1c41fed93",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying a Vertically Shifted and Stretched Exponential Growth Curve",
      "problem": "For the curve $y=1.5({10}^{x})-8.5$, find the point of intersection with the $y-$axis.",
      "worked_solution": "**Method 1**\n\n- For the curve $y={10}^{x},$ the point of intersection with the $y$-axis is $(0,1).$\n\n- For the scaled function $y=1.5({10}^{x}),$ the $y$-coordinate becomes\n\n$$\ny=1.5\\cdot 1=1.5.\n$$\n\n- Finally, after a vertical shift of $8.5$ units down, we get a point with the $y$-coordinate\n\n$$\ny=1.5-8.5=-7.\n$$\n\n**Method 2** \n\nTo find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1.5({10}^{0})-8.5 \\\\  & =1.5\\cdot 1-8.5 \\\\  & =1.5-8.5 \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=1.5({10}^{x})-8.5$ intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,-7).$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(0,-6)",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
